atherClient.get` in `weather.py` now retries when the server returns 503. It makes at most 3 attempts in total, waiting 0.5s after the first failure and 1.0s after the second. I checked it against a real local HTTP server and every case behaved as intended.\n\n- **What gets retried:** only a 503 response. Any other HTTP error, such as 500 or 404, is raised straight away, and so are network errors and timeouts.\n- **When all 3 attempts fail:** the third 503 is raised to the caller as the usual `HTTPError`, with no wait after it.\n- **Constructor change:** `__init__` takes a new optional `sleep` argument, which defaults to `time.sleep`, so tests can skip the real waits. Existing callers don't need to change.\n- **Settings:** the attempt count and starting delay are class constants (`MAX_ATTEMPTS`, `BACKOFF_BASE`), so they're easy to adjust.\n\nThe server's `Retry-After` header is ignored; the client always uses its own fixed delays.\n\nTest results:\n\n| Server responses | Result | Waits |\n|---|---|---|\n| 200 | data returned | none |\n| 503, 200 | data returned | 0.5s |\n| 503, 503, 200 | data returned | 0.5s, 1.0s |\n| 503, 503, 503 | 503 raised after 3 requests | 0.5s, 1.0s |\n| 500 | 500 raised after 1 request | none |\n| 503, 404 | 404 raised | 0.5s |\n\nThe repo has no test suite, so these checks were a one-off script and no test file was added.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 69612, "requests_cache_write": 108604, "requests_cost_usd": 0.5957304000000001, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1937, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial15", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 89, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:49:41.122804+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "